sence, become the queen of all the worlds, like to Sachee of the lord of the celestials and svāhā (An exclamation used in making an oblation to the Gods. A personification of the preceding as the wife of fire and Goddess presiding over burnt offerings.) of the fire. What shall you do with Rama, O Vaidehi, poor and of limited life?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.796,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-23-36"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5022020","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"791ab557630cae6fde1d31a90cfb666284c1a8dba83245ac055417d2eeb28c9f","compact":"5c54691c797283d53b80380c63cd4e0b39a924fe61eb7ad48a6251e3feeff36d","nasal":"ec7f4805943cb0e18890e0af7a66b95a907193a03702c0c811c1ce4fdb9e6922"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-22-21","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":22,"verse":21,"english":"Having your person sprinkled with celestial paste and adorned with excellent ornaments, do you from today O Vaidehī, O you of comely presence, become the queen of all the worlds, like to Sachee of the lord of the celestials and svāhā (An exclamation used in making an oblation to the Gods. A personification of the preceding as the wife of fire and Goddess presiding over burnt offerings.) of the fire. What shall you do with Rama, O Vaidehi, poor and of limited life?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-23-36"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5022021","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"56b297a06cda4b868cb8ea3d2dfccbdc9ca92883d53d04d42131d39d83a4228d","compact":"cdbb35bee3165efb2773eadfa6debb0b52159f6f07e446d06bcba7b952abd9be","nasal":"cdbb35bee3165efb2773eadfa6debb0b52159f6f07e446d06bcba7b952abd9be"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-22-22","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":22,"verse":22,"english":"This is what I say and if do you not follow it we shall all instantly banquet on you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-23-37"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5022022","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5fcd25f8ca9bf45c118b5c10eed31a4b459fe7373473b2408e060282e3b4a6f6","compact":"9c1bd2b4063a94b98dff1b7da0f33ffe7c47535a0abb749ba926f175b3158d0c","nasal":"9c1bd2b4063a94b98dff1b7da0f33ffe7c47535a0abb749ba926f175b3158d0c"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-22-23","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":22,"verse":23,"english":"Thereupon another Rākşasi named Vikață. having her breast hanging long, exercised with ire, and clinching her fist, addressed, roaring, Sita.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.9,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-23-38"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5022023","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d46ca966ced854f9252b21d10a3c27cd25d8f762924b0969745923ffe689af94","compact":"9d06a68f0f08b765e92699dd41439e420cfb89afe03fc6d9a542e394e5fdadf0","nasal":"12bf8762535a22b15a56d84aca135fc5e3b09491464a0afaaba81a0156440fcc"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-22-24","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":22,"verse":24,"english":"O foolish daughter of the king of Mithilā, we have put up with all your foolish words only out of compassion, and because you are a feeble being. It will not lead to your well-being if you do not hear our words. You had been brought here, the other side of the ocean, difficult of being approached by others. You had come within the terrible abode of Rāvana O Maithili, and had been shut up in his room guarded by us all.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.649,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-23-39","DUTT-5-23-40"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5022024","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskr