ve yoll. Do you therefore hear, O Maithili, my well-mcaning words.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.434,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-23-41"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5022027","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"533c0322da10f32ed16494c570d91e92510920c800d71c6b41cbe255ecd136a2","compact":"1065283d224e3b5d026c43bfdd2f34cd18d3c5fd57f5e58f2d04022e6c711ae6","nasal":"1065283d224e3b5d026c43bfdd2f34cd18d3c5fd57f5e58f2d04022e6c711ae6"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-22-28","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":22,"verse":28,"english":"Why do you shed tears? Renounce your useless grief. Do you become happy and delighted, renouncing your continued melancholy.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.349,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-23-42"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5022028","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ac51c18ddf62af4435f7ad217f5be002b00595296b59950ea542157fd3b88135","compact":"0d42259834553015babf3f19b7eb0bd890c65f1f5ae486e8dc98c2f5e35d8bce","nasal":"0d42259834553015babf3f19b7eb0bd890c65f1f5ae486e8dc98c2f5e35d8bce"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-22-29","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":22,"verse":29,"english":"Do you sport, O Sītā, at your pleasure, with the lord of the Rākşasas. We know, for certain, O timid damsel, that the youth of the females, is very transient. And so long as your youth dose not fade, do you pass your days happily, O you having inebriate eyes, with the lord of Rākşasas, in picturesque gardens, and mountain forests. Do you take, O fair damsel, Ravana, the lord of the Rākşasas, for your husband, and thousands of females shall be placed at your service.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.343,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-23-43","DUTT-5-23-44"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5022029","san